e county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 on the middle, January to February came in at 26% of normal, while June to July hit 203%. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, with grid 26548 lowest at 51%. A preliminary estimate on grid 26547 puts August to September 2026 at 161.3, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
